# The committed sample update feed is a REAL Ed25519-signed fixture, not a
# decorative template (see windows/tests/updater/CommittedSampleFeedTests.cs).
# The byte length, SHA-256, and Ed25519 signature recorded in
# appcast-windows.xml / latest-windows.json are ALL computed over the EXACT
# bytes of sample-artifact.txt. If git's autocrlf rewrote LF->CRLF on a Windows
# checkout, the artifact would grow (620 -> 631 bytes) and every pin check would
# fail LengthMismatch-first — flipping the whole suite red on Windows while it
# stays green on macOS. These files MUST therefore be byte-identical on every
# platform, independent of the user's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Treat the signed artifact as binary so its bytes are never touched at all (it
# stands in for a binary MSIX). Pin the feeds + pinned public key to LF so they
# remain byte-identical to what was signed.
sample-artifact.txt    -text
appcast-windows.xml    text eol=lf
latest-windows.json    text eol=lf
pinned-update-key.pub  text eol=lf
